\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Active Perception and Contact Impulse Telemetry.} Temporally aligned network states across contact shock, payload heft, and autonomous transport ($t \in [0, 100]$, $\Delta t = 0.05\,\text  {s}$). Tier 1 (Kinematic Profile): End-effector elevation $y_{\text  {EE}}(t)$ descending during blind approach ($t < 54$), probe impact shock ($t=54$), $+12\,\text  {cm}$ vertical lift probe ($t \in [54, 64]$), and lateral transport. Tier 2 (Population Activity): Spiking raster of the 256-unit ALIF recurrent memory core (Fast Reactive Pool $0..127$, Slow Context Pool $128..255$), demonstrating homeostatic firing rate stability ($\sim 15.4\%$ mean firing rate) without pathological current explosion or burst transients during contact shock ($t=54$). Tier 3 (Handover Authority): Continuous soft-fade blending weight $w_t \in [0.0, 0.40]$ ramping smoothly over 4 frames ($0.10 \to 0.40$) during heft and tapering off ($0.20 \to 0.00$) into autonomous transport. Tier 4 (Momentum Bifurcation): Internalized latent momentum norm $\|\mathbf  {p}_t\|_2$ splitting cleanly by payload mass ($2.04\,\text  {kg}$ vs. $4.07\,\text  {kg}$) into distinct stable plateaus ($\Delta \|\mathbf  {p}_t\| \approx 0.18$), confirming physical inertial internalization.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:telemetry}{{3}{11}{}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Multi-Horizon Stability and Qualitative Drift Ablation.} (a) Grouped log-scale velocity MSE tracking across prediction horizons $H \in \{1, 10, 50, 100\}$. Continuous recurrent baselines (Continuous RSSM, Deep GRU, ConvLSTM, and parameter-matched continuous ANN-Rate) exhibit elevated velocity drift, whereas SPWM maintains strictly bounded error ($0.01153\,\text  {rad}^2/\text  {s}^2$ at $H=100$: $4.2\times $ lower than RSSM, $14.0\times $ lower than GRU). (b) Qualitative 3D scene visualization at horizon $H=100$, displaying the ground-truth payload alongside predictions: SPWM end-effector Cartesian error remains bounded ($\Delta = 6.2\,\text  {cm}$), whereas the continuous rate baseline drifts to $\Delta = 10.4\,\text  {cm}$.}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:stability}{{4}{12}{}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Hardware Efficiency and Physical Domain Boundaries.} (a) Recurrent step compute energy (log-scale nJ/step) and dynamic power (mW at $20\,\text  {Hz}$) comparing Intel Loihi-2 neuromorphic execution (SOPs) against Nvidia Jetson Orin edge GPU execution (MACs). SPWM consumes $12.81\,\text  {nJ/step}$ ($0.256\,\text  {mW}$ dynamic power)—an $80.8\times $ energy advantage over edge GPU execution. (b) 2D sensitivity matrix mapping task grasp success rate across sensor discrepancies (refractory dropout and background noise, demonstrating zero-shot invariance at $74.0\%$--$78.0\%$) versus mechanical mismatch (unmodeled joint friction $\pm 20\%$ and out-of-distribution payload mass $4.80\,\text  {kg}$, exhibiting a sharp drop-off to $14.0\%$--$18.0\%$, isolating the sim-to-real transfer boundary).}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hardware_domain}{{5}{12}{}{figure.5}{}}
